---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="CV — James Sparkes"
  description="CV for James Sparkes, Senior Product Designer."
  path="/cv"
>
  <div class="cv-view">
    <div class="cv-header">
      <div class="cv-name-block">
        <h1 class="cv-name">James Sparkes</h1>
        <div class="cv-role">Senior Product Designer</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="cv-summary">
      Product designer who also ships frontend code. I take products from discovery and research
      through to implementation on a production codebase or with database-driven React prototypes,
      owning the full lifecycle of a product or feature. Most of my work is in
      complex, regulated environments. Currently that means clinical software for fertility
      clinics across the UK, US, Australia and EU, designing for healthcare professionals in
      high-stakes workflows. I care most about reducing friction in the tools people rely on.
    </p>

    <div class="cv-columns">
      <div class="cv-main">
        <div class="cv-block">
          <div class="cv-sec-head">Experience</div>

          <div class="cv-job">
            <div class="cv-job-top">
              <span class="cv-job-title">Product Designer</span>
              <span class="cv-job-dates">Aug 2025 &ndash; Present</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cv-job-meta">wawa fertility <span class="cv-loc">&middot; London / Hybrid</span></div>
            <ul class="cv-points">
              <li>Lead design, prototyping and frontend implementation for clinical-grade software used by fertility clinics across four jurisdictions (UK, US, Australia, EU), each with distinct regulatory standards, owning projects end-to-end in a flat team from discovery through to production code.</li>
              <li>Designed the workflow for automated regulatory reporting, proposing the model behind it and ensuring it can adapt to any country&rsquo;s regulator (PRISM, BORN, SART and ANZARD). Eliminated constant manual checking and data re-entry, with built-in validation keeping data correct before it ever reaches the regulator.</li>
              <li>Designed an end-to-end referral system, effectively a CRM, with a simple intake form and AI-assisted auto-ingestion; clinics report referral handling dropping from 20&ndash;40 minutes to a few minutes, with one going from four referral staff to one.</li>
              <li>Spearheaded a unified questionnaire builder that replaced the survey questions every clinic maintained separately with one system-fed tool, cutting duplicated data entry and surfacing clinically useful information directly to doctors instead of leaving them to hunt for it.</li>
              <li>Instigated the move of the design team from Figma-only to working directly in the production codebase, keeping design integrity intact across flows and the design system, lifting both output and quality while reducing rework for engineers.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="cv-job">
            <div class="cv-job-top">
              <span class="cv-job-title">Senior UX/UI Designer</span>
              <span class="cv-job-dates">Feb 2022 &ndash; Aug 2025</span>
            </div>
            <div class="cv-job-meta">FIXR <span class="cv-loc">&middot; London / Hybrid &middot; incl. freelance 2025</span></div>
            <ul class="cv-points">
              <li>Led end-to-end UX for Timed Entry, a ticketing system that became a major sales driver, cited by 30% of high-revenue prospects as a deciding factor in switching to FIXR.</li>
              <li>Unlocked entirely new verticals (museums, exhibitions, visitor attractions), helping win enterprise organisers worth &pound;100k+ in average annual value from legacy platforms.</li>
              <li>Designed across the full ecosystem, including event creation, checkout, the entry-scanning app and analytics dashboards, keeping a mobile-first experience consistent for both organisers and attendees.</li>
              <li>Extended FIXR&rsquo;s design system with new components, and redesigned organiser onboarding and buyer journeys to improve ticket sales and client retention.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cv-side">
        <div class="cv-side-block">
          <div class="cv-sec-head">Skills</div>
          <div class="cv-skill-group">
            <div class="cv-skill-label">Design</div>
            <div class="cv-skill-items">Product &amp; UX/UI design, design systems, prototyping, design research, interaction design</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cv-skill-group">
            <div class="cv-skill-label">Engineering</div>
            <div class="cv-skill-items">React, Next.js, TypeScript, HTML/CSS, InstantDB</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cv-skill-group">
            <div class="cv-skill-label">Data</div>
            <div class="cv-skill-items">Data cleaning &amp; wrangling, regex, spreadsheet modelling, analysis &amp; charting</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cv-skill-group">
            <div class="cv-skill-label">Tools</div>
            <div class="cv-skill-items">Figma, Linear, GitHub, Git, Claude Code</div>
          </div>
          <div class="cv-skill-group">
            <div class="cv-skill-label">Domains</div>
            <div class="cv-skill-items">Regulated &amp; clinical software, multi-jurisdiction compliance, complex B2B workflows</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cv-side-block">
          <div class="cv-sec-head">Strengths</div>
          <div class="cv-skill-group">
            <div class="cv-skill-items">Designer-engineer hybrid &middot; ships working code &middot; end-to-end ownership &middot; comfortable wrangling and analysing data &middot; designing for high-stakes, error-sensitive contexts</div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="cv-side-block">
          <div class="cv-sec-head">Education</div>
          <div class="cv-edu-item">
            <div class="cv-edu-deg">BA (Hons) Graphic Design &mdash; First Class</div>
            <div class="cv-edu-inst">Canterbury Christ Church University</div>
            <div class="cv-edu-yr">2010&ndash;2013</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
